  "source_contract": {
    "engine_mapping": "Selected callback resolves indices0..44, all within two32-bit A801 chunks. Support and eligible getters use the callback support guards; eligible additionally requires zero aggregate reason mask.",
    "admission": "Stable complete nonzero supported==eligible across64bits; extra high bits remain visible and checked. Zero aggregate mask causes release helper754A10 to return before reason2 count mutation.",
    "ownership": "A separately allocated opposing DISABLE must be rejected exactly. First ENABLE and final release use selector3; current no-reason eligibility is checked. Arbitration is among profiler requests, not exclusive control over all RM mechanisms.",
    "not_generalized": "BLCG and ELPG ENABLE invoke shared reason0 decrement helpers without owner keys; current BLCG register witnesses do not expose count and ELPG current support does not expose complete saved group membership/count. Their standalone ENABLE forms remain unqualified; existing DISABLE controls stay available."
  },
